#%PAM-1.0
# Jarvis OS lock-screen — voice-only path.
#
# Used by `com.jarvis.Lock.VerifyVoice()`. pam_jarvis.so is `required`
# (not `sufficient`) so a voice miss or unavailable daemon fails the
# stack — no silent fallthrough to a password prompt that has no
# stdin behind it. The lock window UI shows the failure verbatim and
# the user can fall back to the password field if they want; we never
# pretend a misfire was a success.
#
# Why not sufficient + system-auth fallback? Because there's no
# password on the wire for this call — the lock daemon's
# VerifyVoice() doesn't pipe one in. A sufficient+fallback stack
# would either block waiting for a non-existent prompt or always
# fail at pam_unix, which is worse UX than a clean voice-verdict.

auth        required     pam_jarvis.so
account     include      system-auth
password    include      system-auth
session     include      system-auth
